You are an expert in TypeScript, React 19, Vite 8, TanStack Router, Redux Toolkit, and CSS modules in this Nx + pnpm monorepo.

## Monorepo

- Package manager: **pnpm** only (`preinstall` enforces it)
- Run tasks via `pnpm nx …` (build, lint, test, serve)
- Apps: `platform` (main), `api-portal`, `data-download-portal`, labelers, `user-groups-admin`
- Shared libs under `libs/` (`ui-components`, `api-client`, `deck-layers`, `dataviews-client`, etc.)

## Response constraints

- Do not remove existing code or comments unless necessary
- Do not reformat imports or unrelated code
- Match surrounding file style (exports, naming, selectors)

## Stack (current)

- **Routing (platform):** TanStack Router + TanStack Start (file routes under `apps/platform/routes/`)
- **Server/async data (platform):** Redux Toolkit + **RTK Query** (`apps/platform/queries/`), `createAsyncThunk` in slices — not TanStack Query
- **Legacy:** `react-query` v3 only in `api-portal`
- **UI:** React 19, CSS modules (`.module.css`), `classnames` as `cx`
- **Utils:** prefer `es-toolkit` over new lodash usage
- **Maps:** deck.gl / MapLibre (layer code is class-based — that is expected)
- **Tests:** Vitest via Nx (`pnpm nx test <project>`)

## Code style

- Functional components; TypeScript throughout; prefer `type` over `interface`
- Descriptive booleans: `isLoading`, `hasError`
- Pure helpers: `function` keyword; curly braces on all conditionals
- Colocate: component + `.module.css` + `*.hooks.ts` + `*.slice.ts` / selectors

## Naming & structure

- Directories: kebab-case (`vessel-groups/`)
- Components: PascalCase files (`Sidebar.tsx`)
- Hooks modules: `Foo.hooks.ts` (not `use-foo.ts` for feature hooks)
- Platform features live under `apps/platform/features/`
- **Apps:** default-export the page/feature component when that is the file’s main export
- **`libs/ui-components`:** named exports (`export function Button`)

## Redux / libs (see scoped rules)

- Platform Redux details: `redux-platform.mdc`
- deck.gl layers: `deck-layers.mdc`
- Shared UI: `ui-components.mdc`

## Performance

- Prefer efficient data fetching (RTK Query cache, abort signals) and avoid unnecessary re-renders
- Do not add `useMemo` / `useCallback` by default unless the file already relies on them or profiling shows a need (React Compiler is not enabled yet)
